        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "3-Methoxysalicylaldehyde (0.47 g, 3.1 mmol) was dissolved in 20 mL of water. Cesium hydroxide (0.89 g, 5.3 mmol) was added and the solution was heated for 10 min while being stirred. Gadolinium(III) nitrate pentahydrate (1.34 g, 3.1 mmol) was then added. The yellow precipitate was stirred at room temperature overnight, filtered off, washed with water, and dried under vacuum to leave a yellow powder (0.26 g, 20%). Crystals of the same material were obtained by slow evaporation of a solution containing L'Gd (L' = deprotonated tris[4-(2-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenyl)-3-aza-3-butenyl]amine) dissolved in dichloromethane and an alcohol-water (1/1) solution of Gd(NO3)3·6H2O; analytical and spectroscopic data matched the powdered sample.",
